    'faq.title': "FAQ \u2014 How to use OPR Card Generator - Redesign",
    'faq.callout': "<strong>Read this first:</strong> your list only loads if you shared it in Army Forge. Open your army there, click <strong>\u201CShare as Link\u201D</strong>, and paste that link (or its list ID) here. A list that was never shared cannot be read and will fail to load.",
    'faq.lead': 'Read this first:',
    'faq.leadSuffix': " your list only loads if you shared it in Army Forge. Open your army there, click <strong>\u201CShare as Link\u201D</strong>, and paste that link (or its list ID) here. A list that was never shared cannot be read and will fail to load.",
    'faq.generateQ': 'How do I generate cards?',
    'faq.generateA': "In Army Forge, open your army and click <strong>\u201CShare as Link\u201D</strong>. Copy the link it gives you, paste it into the box on the Home page (the bare list ID also works), and click <strong>Generate Cards</strong>. If you\u2019ve loaded that list before, it opens instantly from your saved copy \u2014 no download needed.",
    'faq.outdatedQ': "My cards look out of date \u2014 how do I update them?",
    'faq.outdatedA': "Cards open from your saved copy for speed, so changes you made in Army Forge afterwards won\u2019t show until you re-download the list. Click <strong>Refresh List</strong> on the Home page (or <strong>Refresh</strong> in <strong>My Lists</strong>) to pull the latest version from Army Forge and update your saved copy.",
    'faq.wontLoadQ': "Why won\u2019t my list load?",
    'faq.wontLoadA': "By far the most common reason is that the list was never shared. Go back to Army Forge and click <strong>\u201CShare as Link\u201D</strong> \u2014 without it, the list is private and can\u2019t be read. Also double-check that you copied the whole link (or the correct list ID).",
    'faq.bgQ': 'How do I add a background image to a card?',
    'faq.bgA': "Click a card to pick an image (up to <strong>2 MB</strong>). Once it has one, <strong>drag</strong> (or use the <strong>Horizontal</strong> / <strong>Vertical</strong> sliders) to reposition, <strong>scroll</strong> (or use the Zoom slider) to zoom, and use the Opacity slider to fade it. <strong>Recenter</strong> resets the framing, and the <strong>\u2715</strong> removes the image.",
    'faq.savedQ': 'Are my background images saved?',
    'faq.savedA': "Yes. Each image \u2014 with its zoom, position and opacity \u2014 is stored on your device for that unit, so it\u2019s still there when you reload. When you <strong>Refresh List</strong> the image stays as long as the unit is still in the list; if a unit is removed (or you delete the list), its image is cleaned up automatically. Removing an image with the <strong>\u2715</strong> deletes it too. Images are kept on your device only \u2014 they aren\u2019t uploaded anywhere.",
    'faq.combineQ': 'What does "Combine similar units" do?',
    'faq.combineA': "With this option on, identical units are merged into one card prefixed with their count \u2014 three of the same unit show as <strong>3x</strong> on a single card instead of three copies, with the model count shown as <strong>[5]</strong> after the name. This works for any unit regardless of model count, and up to three identical units share a card (a fourth starts a new one). Combining is purely cosmetic to save paper \u2014 points and loadout stay at the single-unit values. It\u2019s off by default, so every unit shows on its own card unless you turn it on.",
    'faq.customQ': 'What does "Use custom unit names" do?',
    'faq.customA': "With this option on, a unit you\u2019ve renamed in Army Forge shows that custom name (e.g. <strong>Frodo</strong>) as the card title, and the original book name moves to the subtitle. It\u2019s on by default; turn it off to show the default book name as the title.",
    'faq.printQ': 'How do I print?',
    'faq.printA': 'Click <strong>Print</strong>. Use the checkboxes above the cards to choose what goes on the page: the cards, the special rules table, and the spells table.',
    'faq.downloadQ': 'How do I download the cards?',
    'faq.downloadA': 'Each card has a <strong>PNG</strong> button to download it on its own.',
    'faq.listsQ': 'What is "My Lists"?',
    'faq.listsA': 'Every list you generate is saved automatically on your device. From <strong>My Lists</strong> you can <strong>Load</strong> one instantly from your saved copy, <strong>Refresh</strong> it to pull the latest version from Army Forge (this only happens when you click it), or <strong>Delete</strong> it. Loading a list also restores the options you had set for it (such as <strong>Combine similar units</strong>).',
    'changelog.title': 'Changelog',
    'changelog.intro': "What\u2019s new in OPR Card Generator - Redesign. Newest changes first.",
    'about.title': 'About',
    'about.lead': 'A small web app that turns a shared <a href="https://army-forge.onepagerules.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Army Forge</a> list into printable unit cards for <a href="https://onepagerules.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OnePageRules</a> games.',
    'about.text1': "Paste a shared army link, get one card per unit (stats, special rules, weapons), plus a combined special-rules table and a spells table \u2014 ready to print or download as PNGs.",
    'about.note': "<strong>Note:</strong> a list only loads if you shared it in Army Forge \u2014 open your army and click <strong>\u201CShare as Link\u201D</strong> first. Private (unshared) lists cannot be read.",
    'about.forkText': '<strong>This project is a fork of OPR Card Generator by JeanOmeg.</strong> Thank you, JeanOmeg, for creating and sharing the original project with the community.',
    'about.forkRepo': '<a href="https://github.com/JeanOmeg/opr-card-generator" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original GitHub repository</a>',
    'about.forkSite': '<a href="https://jeanomeg.github.io/opr-card-generator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original online app</a>',
    'about.forkIssues': '<a href="https://github.com/JeanOmeg/opr-card-generator/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Issues and suggestions</a>',
    'about.forkReleases': '<a href="https://github.com/JeanOmeg/opr-card-generator/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original project releases</a>',
    'about.forkLicense': '<a href="https://github.com/JeanOmeg/opr-card-generator/blob/master/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Original project license</a>',
    'about.forkAuthor': '<a href="https://github.com/JeanOmeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JeanOmeg on GitHub</a>',
    'about.features': 'Features',
    'about.featureCards': 'One printable card per unit: Quality / Defense / Tough, special rules, weapons, notes.',
    'about.featureTables': 'Combined <strong>special-rules table</strong> (including core/common rule descriptions) and a <strong>spells table</strong> for casters.',
    'about.featureBg': "Per-card <strong>background image</strong> (up to 2 MB) with drag- or slider-based positioning, scroll/slider zoom, opacity and recenter \u2014 saved on your device per unit and kept across refreshes.",
    'about.featurePrint': '<strong>Print</strong> layout (choose cards / rules / spells) and <strong>PNG</strong> download (single or all).',
    'about.featureLists': "<strong>My Lists</strong> \u2014 every generated list is saved locally on your device so you can reload it instantly, refresh it on demand, or delete it.",
    'about.featureCache': "<strong>Cache-first loading</strong> \u2014 Generate Cards opens a previously loaded list instantly from your saved copy (works offline); use <strong>Refresh List</strong> to pull the latest version from Army Forge.",
    'about.featurePages': '<strong>FAQ</strong>, <strong>Changelog</strong>, and <strong>About</strong> pages.',
    'about.disclaimer': 'Disclaimer',
    'about.disclaimer1': 'This is a <strong>free, non-profit project made by a fan, for fans</strong>. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by OnePageRules.',
    'about.disclaimer2': 'OnePageRules and all of its game systems, rules, and content (Grimdark Future, Age of Fantasy, and others) are the property of <strong>OnePageRules</strong>. This tool only helps players display their own army lists, and is offered free of charge for non-commercial community use.',
    'about.license': 'License',
